[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is a Path Traversal (also known as Zip Slip, though applied to tar files here). This vulnerability occurs because the code constructs the full extraction path by directly concatenating the user-supplied destination path with the filename retrieved from the archive (`archive_entry_pathname(entry)`). If a malicious archive contains filenames with path traversal sequences (e.g., `../../evil.txt`), the `snprintf` operation will create a path that points outside the intended extraction directory, potentially allowing an attacker to write or overwrite arbitrary files on the file system.

